From 05926fa332323593b87dc8d8efb8cd2eb2e9695c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:24:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: look-alike flags, Normal and Hard answers, and a Pick
 the flag quiz

Flag-based quizzes (Flag to Country, Pick the flag, Speed Round) now put flags that people really
confuse among the wrong answers. FlagLookAlikes maps each country to its classic look-alikes (curated:
Chad and Romania, Indonesia and Monaco, Ireland and Ivory Coast, the Nordic crosses, ...) followed by
the nearest flags by image similarity, generated by tools/gen-lookalikes.py from the shipped artwork
(Lab colour distance, also trying mirrored, flipped and turned versions). Normal puts one look-alike
among the three wrong answers, Hard as many as exist; look-alikes outside the quiz scope are never
offered, and Hard fills with random countries when a flag has few. Capital and continent questions
are unchanged.

Pick the flag shows a country's name and four flags to choose from, in a new FlagOptionGrid that keeps
the option tags, result colours and screen reader descriptions of the text options. The setup screen
gets an Answers row (Normal or Hard) that is inactive for questions without flags, and the score
screen says which difficulty was played.

The existing quiz UI tests now scroll to the Start button before using setup controls: the fifth mode
card pushed the scope chips under the bottom bar, where a tap on them was swallowed, so some tests were
quietly running on the Global scope.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
